{"year":"2021","content":[{"type":"text","content_text":"The 78th Golden Globe Awards ceremony was held on February 28, 2021, almost two months later than usual because of the COVID-19 pandemic. For the first time the show was hosted from two coasts: <a href=\"https://_{type: 'screen', 'id': 56323, 'screen_type': person}\">Tina Fey</a> in New York, at the Rainbow Room, and <a href=\"https://_{type: 'screen', 'id': 56322, 'screen_type': person}\">Amy Poehler</a> at the Beverly Hilton in Beverly Hills, broadcast by NBC. <a href=\"https://_{type: 'screen', 'id': 581734, 'screen_type': movie}\">Nomadland</a> (2021) won Best Motion Picture – Drama and gave <a href=\"https://_{type: 'screen', 'id': 1395183, 'screen_type': person}\">Chloé Zhao</a> the Director award, while <a href=\"https://_{type: 'screen', 'id': 740985, 'screen_type': movie}\">Borat Subsequent Moviefilm: Delivery of Prodigious Bribe to American Regime for Make Benefit Once Glorious Nation of Kazakhstan</a> (2020) took Best Motion Picture – Musical or Comedy. <a href=\"https://_{type: 'screen', 'id': 172069, 'screen_type': person}\">Chadwick Boseman</a> posthumously received the award for Best Actor in a Motion Picture – Drama for <a href=\"https://_{type: 'screen', 'id': 615667, 'screen_type': movie}\">Ma Rainey's Black Bottom</a> (2020). <i>Television awards are not included.</i>"},{"type":"awards_nominees","name":"Best Motion Picture – Drama","nominee_list":[{"type":"movie","id":581734,"name":"Nomadland","image_path":"/pLwarSuyUjw6vF0U6JhlHzAa1Gp.jpg","director":"Chloé Zhao","winner":true,"backdrop_path":"/563sRDK3rZS31TXCdTY4lfcwrNK.jpg"},{"type":"movie","id":600354,"name":"The Father","image_path":"/85d7NFk3BnoaJr1NnH3gLl2lRCU.jpg","director":"Florian Zeller","winner":false},{"type":"movie","id":614560,"name":"Mank","image_path":"/gyjYToNFFIUKUvBYFchqpptZA1F.jpg","director":"David Fincher","winner":false},{"type":"movie","id":582014,"name":"Promising Young Woman","image_path":"/r7FwclLTWB8i6XfBNTtUsy